{"content":[{"c":["MESHECH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Son of Japheth and Noah’s grandson (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.2","r":"Gen.10.2","rawR":"Gen.10.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.2","value":"Gen.10.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:2"},"). His descendants are usually mentioned in connection with Tubal, Gog, or Magog (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.120.5","r":"Ps.120.5","rawR":"Ps.120.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.120.5","value":"Ps.120.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 120:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.13","r":"Ezek.27.13","rawR":"Ezek.27.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.13","value":"Ezek.27.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 27:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.32.26","r":"Ezek.32.26","rawR":"Ezek.32.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.32.26","value":"Ezek.32.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"32:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.38.2-3","r":"Ezek.38.2-3","rawR":"Ezek.38.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.38.2-3","value":"Ezek.38.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"38:2-3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.39.1","r":"Ezek.39.1","rawR":"Ezek.39.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.39.1","value":"Ezek.39.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"39:1"},"). They are called Muski in Assyrian records and inhabited the mountains north of Assyria during the reigns of Tiglath-pileser I (1115–1102 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), Shalmaneser III (859–824 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), and Sargon (722–705 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). The people of Meshech are characterized as aggressive and pagan, traders in bronze and slaves with Tyre."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Shem’s son according to ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.17","r":"1Chr.1.17","rawR":"1Chr.1.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.17","value":"1Chr.1.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 1:17"},", but rendered Mash in the parallel passage in ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.23","r":"Gen.10.23","rawR":"Gen.10.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.23","value":"Gen.10.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 10:23"},". The latter is generally accepted."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Meshech","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.2","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.2","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.2"},{"anchorText":"Ps 120:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.120.5","rawQueryValue":"Ps.120.5","sourceRefExact":"Ps.120.5"},{"anchorText":"Ez 27:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.27.13","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.27.13","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.27.13"},{"anchorText":"32:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.32.26","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.32.26","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.32.26"},{"anchorText":"38:2-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.38.2-3","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.38.2-3","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.38.2-3"},{"anchorText":"39:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.39.1","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.39.1","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.39.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 1:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.17","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.17","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.17"},{"anchorText":"Genesis 10:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.23","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.23","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.23"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"914678d1da187fe8c26b236f3e4659ef43c9de3fdb218075c4aec8b11b984487","sourceItemName":"Meshech","sourceItemOrder":273,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Meshech","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Meshech","title":"Meshech","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}